## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "2000mA"
  total_current_limit: "500mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "1769-L30ER has NO integrated field I/O and NO built-in power supply — a separate 1769-PA or 1769-PB power supply module MUST be installed immediately to the left of the controller on the DIN rail or panel; without the power supply the CPU will not power on; the power supply must be ordered separately (1769-PA2 for 120/240VAC or 1769-PB2 for 24VDC)"
    - "Both EtherNet/IP ports on the 1769-L30ER share a SINGLE IP address via an embedded 2-port switch — do NOT configure the two ports with different IP addresses; for network isolation between segments use a separate managed switch or a second network adapter; the embedded DLR switch enables ring topology without a managed switch but does not provide VLAN separation"
    - "The 1769-L30ER (non-M variant) does NOT support Integrated Motion on EtherNet/IP (CIP Motion) — motion control requires the 1769-L30ERM variant; the L30ER can still control simple drives via MSG instructions or third-party drives via EtherNet/IP but without the full CIP Motion trajectory planner; substituting L30ER for L30ERM in a motion application will cause axis configuration errors in Studio 5000"
    - "The 1769-L30ER DOES include an internal energy-storage supercapacitor (RTC holdup ~35 days at 25°C) — the 1769-L30ER-NSE variant (No Stored Energy) deliberately OMITS this supercapacitor and provides NO RTC backup after power loss; select the correct variant for your application; confusing L30ER and L30ER-NSE in a time-critical system will cause clock loss on every power failure"
    - "Maximum local expansion modules is 8 × 1769 Compact I/O modules, but the power supply distance rating is 4 — this means a maximum of 3 I/O modules may be placed between the controller and the power supply before another power supply must be installed; exceeding the power supply distance rating causes backplane communication errors and unpredictable I/O module faults"
    - "The 1784-SD1 (1 GB) SD card shipped with the controller is REQUIRED for program storage on power cycle — if the SD card is removed or corrupted the controller will not reload the program on power-up; do NOT remove the SD card during RUN mode; use only Rockwell Automation 1784-SD1 or 1784-SD2 cards; third-party SD cards are NOT supported and will cause memory integrity faults"
    - "The USB port on the 1769-L30ER is for TEMPORARY programming use only (not intended for permanent industrial connection) — do not use the USB port as a permanent network interface; isolation is 30VDC continuous Basic Insulation; the USB port is NOT isolated from the system in the same way Ethernet ports are; always use EtherNet/IP for permanent network topology"
    - "EtherNet/IP node count limit is 16 for the 1769-L30ER (versus 32 for L33ER and up to 80 for L38ERM) — each distributed I/O adapter, drive, and EtherNet/IP device consumes one node count; if the application requires more than 16 nodes a larger controller (L33ER or above) or a secondary Logix controller on the network must be used; node count is per controller, not per port"
    - "The 1769 Compact I/O system requires a 1769-ECR (right end cap) on the rightmost module in the system — failure to install the end cap leaves the backplane bus open and causes backplane communication faults across all I/O modules; the end cap is included with the controller but must be physically transferred to the last I/O module when expansion modules are added"
compatibility:
  sw: "Studio 5000 Logix Designer V21+ (primary); RSLogix 5000 V16-V20 (legacy); FactoryTalk View SE/ME for HMI; RSLinx Classic or FactoryTalk Linx for comms"
  languages: "Relay Ladder (LD);Function Block Diagram (FBD);Structured Text (ST);Sequential Function Chart (SFC)"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;EtherNet-IP-CIP;CIP-Sync;CIP-Safety-read;DLR;DeviceNet-via-1769-SDN;PCCC;Studio5000;FactoryTalk"
  certifications: "cULus;CE;UKCA;RCM;IECEx;ATEX-Zone2;KC;CCC;EtherNet-IP-ODVA"

